KG42.register("clusters-2387b10bb5587d996223406c",{"id":"02-dlmp::v142-d-CL002","paper":"02-dlmp","label":"Hourly energy purchasing by price-taking aggregators and conditional decentralized implementation","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL002","label":"Hourly energy purchasing by price-taking aggregators and conditional decentralized implementation","market_meaning":"A price-taking aggregator controlling a small number of EVs chooses hourly energy-purchase quantities to minimize charging costs, given nodal DLMP and charging and SOC conditions. Central clearing and pricing serve as input interfaces and benchmarks for efficiency comparisons; the source supports the central optimal charging schedule also being optimal for the aggregator when constraint (7) is nonbinding, but gaps remain in the conditions under which an arbitrary autonomous response recovers that allocation.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["DEM","LEM"],"process_stages":["clearing","coordination","participation","pricing"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The LEM annotation in R007 and the DEM annotations in the other chains are all retained as written. The interface is based on the explicit semantics of hourly EV charging purchases within the same mechanism and does not thereby equate the two market types. Prices are endogenous on the DSO side and given on the aggregator side; central nodal aggregate quantities remain distinct from individual response quantities. The efficiency link is subject to conditions including price-taking behavior, a common physical scope, and constraint (7) being nonbinding.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Combines participant behavioral assumptions, hourly commodity quantities, and autonomous cost minimization into a response rule with explicit inputs, a responsible actor, and energy-purchase outputs. Central welfare clearing and price formation serve only as shared interfaces and a basis for comparison; their repeated formulations are not counted as additional independent rules.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides aggregator optimization under given DLMP, information requirements, and an interpretation of decentralized responses, constituting this cluster's autonomous energy-purchasing decision."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"States the assumptions of no market power and price-taking behavior, explaining why aggregators treat published prices as given inputs."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R007","ownership":"primary","role":"interface","rationale":"Interprets the response decision as hourly purchases of EV charging energy and retains the local formulations of commodity quantities and their upper bounds."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"shared","role":"support","rationale":"Shares central feasibility conditions, the EV dual-price formulation, and the efficiency link as benchmarks for comparison; its central clearing remains primarily assigned to v142-d-CL001."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"shared","role":"support","rationale":"Shares the social welfare objective and the discussion of decentralized implementation to explain the conditional link between responses and the social optimum, without duplicating ownership of the central optimization rule."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R006","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Shares the DLMP produced by the DSO as the source of the aggregator's given prices and retains the conditions for price formation."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-L01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-theta01","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E27","v141-b-g01-E28","v141-b-g01-E30"],"rationale":"The participation assumptions of a small share and no market power correspond to the behavior of choosing energy-purchase quantities under given DLMP; this is a modeling condition in the source, not a newly added market-entry procedure."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-L02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R006::x::x_P_DLMP"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-theta01","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g01-E30","v141-b-g01-E37"],"rationale":"The nodal DLMP calculated and sent by the DSO becomes the given price in aggregator optimization. The connection retains the two local roles of endogenous price and response parameter without rewriting them as a single variable."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-L03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R007::x::x_ev_charging_energy_i_t","v141-c-R007::theta::E_ev_charging_limit_i_t","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x01","v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-theta02","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E28","v141-b-g01-E29","v141-b-g01-E30"],"rationale":"E30 directly interprets the charging quantity chosen by the aggregator as energy purchased each hour, linking the commodity definition to the optimization output; the commodity upper bound cannot replace the complete SOC constraints."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-L04","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-001","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C005"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x01","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E25","v141-b-g01-E33","v141-b-g01-E34"],"rationale":"Theorem 1 and its proof connect a central optimal charging schedule satisfying the conditions to the aggregator's set of optimal solutions. This link supports the compatibility of optimal schedules; it does not prove that every optimal response equals the central schedule."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-L05","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02","v141-b-g01-E35","v141-b-g01-E36","v141-b-g01-E38"],"rationale":"Corollary 1 incorporates EV responses and conventional demand into a conditional interpretation of decentralized implementation, so welfare outcomes and response behavior can be functionally assembled; conventional-demand determinacy and consistency of selection still require separate verification."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-L06","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","kind":"alternative_representation","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C008"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E29","v141-b-g01-E30"],"rationale":"The two occurrences retain clearing and commodity formulations of the charging upper-bound relationship. These are alternative expressions requiring alignment of actors and aggregation bases, and should not be counted as an additional independent rule on the basis of a repeated upper bound."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-O01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R004::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g01-E26","v141-b-g01-E30","v141-b-g01-E37"],"rationale":"These nodes all refer to the local DLMP pricing function through which prices are formed and used for charging responses within the same mechanism; the display representative is kept consistent with that of the central cluster."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-O02","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R002::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R004::V::coordination.price_signal"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R001::V::coordination.price_signal","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02","v141-b-g01-E35","v141-b-g01-E38"],"rationale":"All three occurrences refer to the function of DLMP in coordinating decentralized responses. Only display identity is unified, while each chain's distinct discussion of clearing, welfare, and information conditions is retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-O03","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R006::x::x_P_DLMP","v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-theta01"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g01-E30","v141-b-g01-E37"],"rationale":"The source explicitly passes the DLMP published by the DSO for the same node and period to the aggregator. The central endogenous price and the aggregator's exogenous parameter are retained separately; their local roles cannot be merged."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-O04","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x01","v141-c-R007::x::x_ev_charging_energy_i_t"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E28","v141-b-g01-E29","v141-b-g01-E30"],"rationale":"Within the same aggregator-response scope, the optimized charging quantity is the hourly energy-purchase commodity quantity; object bindings for the response decision and commodity quantity are retained separately."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-O05","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-theta02","v141-c-R007::theta::E_ev_charging_limit_i_t"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E29","v141-b-g01-E30"],"rationale":"Within the same scope of hourly charging purchases, the two objects correspond to the same upper bound, used respectively for the response feasible set and the commodity interpretation; the charging power in the case study has not been directly assigned to the energy upper bound."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-O06","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C008","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E29","v141-b-g01-E30"],"rationale":"The two objects express charging upper bounds of the same form but are bound respectively to a central nodal quantity and an energy-purchase commodity quantity. The actors and aggregation bases still require checking, so they are retained only as related alternative formulations, without declaring the constraints fully duplicative."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G01","category":"math_incomplete","description":"Theorem 1 supports the central optimal charging schedule also being optimal for the aggregator; linear optimization at given prices may have multiple optimal solutions. The frozen chains do not provide uniqueness or coordinated-selection conditions, so cost minimization cannot establish that all autonomous responses recover the central allocation and network feasibility.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E30","v141-b-g01-E33","v141-b-g01-E34","v141-b-g01-E35","v141-b-g01-E36","v141-b-g01-E38"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check whether the source provides uniqueness, optimal-solution selection, or other sufficient conditions, distinguishing the existence of an implementable schedule from a guarantee for arbitrary responses; if the source does not provide these, continue to retain this gap explicitly."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G02","category":"upstream_missing","description":"Decentralized implementation also involves conventional demand, but the existing chains contain no independent household or retailer response optimization or its uniqueness conditions. E36's statement on demand determinacy cannot follow automatically from the general inverse demand function in R002 alone, nor can the linear demand specification in the case study be generalized to the full scope.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-c","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-p-P","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g01-E35","v141-b-g01-E36","v141-b-g01-E38","v141-b-g02-E18"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Have the upstream stage check source support for conventional-demand responses, inverse-demand properties, and the retailer's role, and specify the applicable conditions; until then, retain complete decentralized implementation as a conditional candidate."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G03","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The aggregator's SOC conditions likewise use cumulative charging before the current period, without specifying end-of-day closure or the contribution of charging in the final period to meeting demand. This is the response-side manifestation of the same planning-horizon boundary issue as v142-d-CL001-G05.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C009","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g01-E29"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Jointly check the time horizons, SOC timing, and prerequisites for meeting intraday requirements in the central and aggregator models; supplement subsequent C versions only according to the source, without adding terminal constraints through D."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G04","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The aggregation basis linking central nodal aggregate charging quantities and individual aggregator responses is unspecified. If multiple aggregators exist at the same node, each response cannot be directly equated with the nodal total; the units and period conversions for energy-purchase quantities and upper bounds are also incomplete. At present, identity is linked only internally within central quantities and within response commodity quantities, separately.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-001","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-x","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x01","v141-c-R007::x::x_ev_charging_energy_i_t","v141-c-R007::theta::E_ev_charging_limit_i_t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E27","v141-b-g01-E29","v141-b-g01-E30","v141-b-g01-E33"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the correspondence among node, fleet, aggregator, and time indices, together with the dimensions, before deciding whether quantity identity across actors can be established further; do not merge solely on the basis of identical symbols."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G05","category":"unverified_source","description":"All supporting materials remain unverified experimental candidates and have not undergone independent source or C2 review. In addition, the g01 and g02 transcriptions differ in the demand dual terms and the set of nonfinal periods in (36)/(37), and (45)/(46) also contain duplicate entries; these cannot support a claim that a complete optimality proof has been closed.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C005","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E24","v141-b-g01-E25","v141-b-g01-E27","v141-b-g01-E30","v141-b-g01-E31","v141-b-g01-E33","v141-b-g01-E35","v141-b-g02-E05","v141-b-g02-E06","v141-b-g02-E11"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually inspect this cluster and all referenced chains item by item, and check the numbering, dual terms, and indices of the relevant original formulas; retain the C content from this round, without substituting D assembly for source auditing or scientific confirmation."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G06","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The aggregator's intermediary identity and price-taking behavior are currently represented by existing participation and coordination objects, while the related proposals for dedicated nodes remain unapproved. The assembly has neither treated the aggregator as the DSO nor introduced an energy-supply or V2G role.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R005::V::participation.consumer","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E27","v141-b-g02-E07","v141-b-g03-E03"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-prop-ev-aggregator","v141-b-g02-P01","v141-b-g03-P01"],"required_work":"Manually decide whether the aggregator identity and price-taking conditions require an ontology extension, and address overlapping proposals; continue to reference only existing objects until approval."}]},"rule_refs":["02-dlmp::v141-c-R004","02-dlmp::v141-c-R005","02-dlmp::v141-c-R007","02-dlmp::v141-c-R001","02-dlmp::v141-c-R002","02-dlmp::v141-c-R006"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-276b46f772c03e0a","COMP-5e870d267afec9a0","COMP-80212c4bda48caf5","COMP-ab3d11c48c98c7be","COMP-c6917f781ea3f39e","COMP-fe1ce5f5844f5ec1","KG31-32e2e028530561b5"]});
